Acknowledgements:
    - lecture slides, UMASM examples on the course website
    - TA's in OH
        Catherine for help with maximum negative numbers


Compile and run:
    - Compile using
        ./compile

    - Run using
        um calc40.um

            or

        um calc40.um < [INPUT FILE]


Implemented:
    - The implementation runs as expected, there are no known bugs
    - All calculator operations were implemented successfully including
      special cases and error handling.


Explanations: 
    - Departures: 
        There are no departures from the recommended calling conventions.
        
    - Print Module:
        The print module is implemented using recursion as recommended in the 
        spec by breaking down each number into digits, storing them in a 
        temporary stack r2, and then printing them in order after handling 
        special cases like zero and negatives.

    - Value Stack:
        The value stack is represented as valuestack with r5 pointing to the
        top of the stack.

    - Sections:
        urt0.ums:
            .section init: 
                Initialize the environment for the RPN program - set register r0
                to be 0, reserve temporary registers r6 and r7, and set register
                r2 as the stack pointer and r5 as the base pointer.  

            .section data: 
                Initializes and reserves space in memory for the 
                value stack and the end stack for the RPN program.
        
        calc40.ums:
            .section init: 
                Sets up memory and mapping before the program runs, 
                initializes the jumptable, and sets up stack addresses.

            .section rodata: 
                Allocates a block of 256 bytes of memory for the jumptable.

            .section text: 
                Contains the executable code for the functions
                of the operators, input handling for waiting and entering, error
                handling for input and operators, and stack operations.

        printd.ums:
            .section init: 
                Initalizes registers and temporary registers (r6, r7, r0), 
                and sets up the jumptable to call the print function - 
                maps the newline character in the jumptable to the print_d
                function so that pressing enter cause the value on the stack
                to be printed.
                
            .section text: 
                implements the print module - contains the executable code for 
                recursively printing each number on the value stack in the 
                correct format and handles special cases like zero and negative 
                numbers.

        callmain.ums:
            .section init: Calls the main function to run the program and 
            halts the program after main returns.